      "writtenOn": "2018-01-12T19:28:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it by design, since v2 allows additional signer(s)?  What\u0027s the implication if both v2 and v3 exist, with additional signer of v2?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 953,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 953,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "3c034107ab60200e64d831eac6c86c2e0d79b7c7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "85745b90_745d1065",
        "filename": "src/main/java/com/android/apksig/ApkSigner.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 953,
      "author": {
        "id": 1026058
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-12T21:44:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is by design.  Due to the lack of use of multiple signers in the wild, and the complexity involved with maintaining key rotation between multiple certificates, we\u0027re not supporting it with v3.  A multi-signed v2 apk can never be a v3-signed apk.",
      "parentUuid": "fed4bb54_87447bea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 953,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 953,
        "endChar": 71
      },
